const collectionIntros:Record<string,string>={
 calculators:'Profitability calculators help owners test whether sales, costs, and fees support a sustainable business. Use the profit margin calculator to see how much revenue remains after product costs, the break-even calculator to estimate the unit sales needed to cover fixed and variable costs, and the late-payment fee calculator to model a contract-based estimate. These tools are useful when reviewing product performance, planning a launch, or checking how changes in costs affect a target. Enter figures in a consistent currency and treat outputs as planning estimates, not accounting or legal advice. Pair these results with pricing tools when you need to turn a target into a selling price.',
 'pricing-calculators':'Pricing calculators help you set, compare, and adjust prices with a clearer view of the numbers behind each decision. Use the markup calculator to add a percentage to cost, the selling price calculator to work backward from a target profit margin, and the discount calculator to estimate customer savings. These tools are useful for preparing a price list, testing a promotion, or checking whether a proposed price meets your goals. Margin and markup use different bases, so choose the calculation that matches the question you are asking. Results are estimates; account separately for overhead, taxes, shipping, and other costs that are not part of your inputs.',
 'freelancer-tools':'Freelancer tools support practical planning for rates, project estimates, working time, and pay comparisons. Use the hourly rate calculator to account for income goals, business expenses, and realistic billable hours; the project pricing calculator to combine estimated time and costs; and the hours tools to separate paid work from breaks or compare hourly pay with a salary equivalent. They are useful when setting a new rate, preparing a quote, reviewing capacity, or tracking a shift. Start with realistic assumptions: not every working hour is billable, and project scope can change. Use the results as a starting point, then check them against your own expenses and client agreements.',
 'business-documents':'Business document generators help freelancers and small businesses prepare clear invoices, quotations, and receipts without starting from a blank page. Add your business and customer details, list the work or items, and review the preview before printing or saving a PDF. Use an invoice after requesting payment, a quotation to describe proposed work and pricing before it begins, and a receipt to record a completed payment. These tools are useful for routine client administration and keeping documents consistent. The generators do not determine tax treatment, legal requirements, or payment terms; check local rules and your agreement with the customer. Document details stay in your browser during editing.',
 'marketing-tools':'The UTM link builder adds campaign labels to a destination URL so analytics reports can distinguish traffic sources, channels, and campaigns. Use it when sharing links in newsletters, social posts, ads, or partner placements and you want to compare their performance. Enter a valid landing-page address, then add consistent source, medium, and campaign values; optional term and content fields help distinguish keywords or creative variations. Preview and copy the finished URL before publishing it. Agree on naming conventions with your team to avoid splitting one campaign across multiple labels. Keep personal or confidential information out of UTM values because they become part of the shared URL.',
 'video-tools':'Video tools help you prepare clips locally in your browser. The video trimmer exports a selected section, while the PC-only video upscaler applies a local AI super-resolution model to compatible frames. Processing, codec and hardware support vary by file and desktop browser.',
 'pdf-tools':'PDF tools help you prepare and inspect common document changes directly in your browser. Merge files into one packet, split selected pages, rotate pages, add page numbers or a watermark, convert images to PDF, or export PDF pages as JPGs. Compression is available for cases where an image-based document is acceptable; it rasterizes page content, so text may no longer be searchable. These tools are useful for assembling forms, sharing selected pages, and preparing files for review or printing. Choose the tool that matches the task, inspect the generated preview, and download only after checking the result. Files are processed on your device rather than uploaded to Digitalivez servers.',
 'image-tools':'Image tools help you prepare visual assets for documents, websites, and social platforms. Resize or crop an image to fit a target, convert between browser-supported formats, reduce file size, create favicon files, generate social-media dimensions, or upscale an image with a local AI super-resolution model. Use the compressor when a smaller file is important, the resizer when exact dimensions matter, and the cropper or platform presets when framing needs to change. Preview the actual output and confirm that text, transparency, and image quality remain suitable before downloading. Format support can vary by browser, especially for AVIF and WebP. Images are processed locally in your browser and are not sent to Digitalivez servers.'
}
const collectionRelatedGuideRoutes:Record<string,string[]>={calculators:['/guides/profit-margin-vs-markup','/guides/business-break-even-point','/guides/price-products-for-profit','/guides/business-pricing-mistakes'],'pricing-calculators':['/guides/profit-margin-vs-markup','/guides/price-products-for-profit','/guides/business-pricing-mistakes','/guides/discounts-and-profit-margins'],'freelancer-tools':['/guides/freelancer-hourly-rates','/guides/calculate-billable-hours','/guides/calculate-project-costs'],'business-documents':['/guides/calculate-project-costs'],'marketing-tools':['/guides/utm-parameters-campaign-tracking']}
